What is Pycnogenol?

Pycnogenol is a patented natural extract derived from the bark of the French maritime pine tree (Pinus pinaster). It contains a unique blend of procyanidins, bioflavonoids, and organic acids, known for their potent antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties. While primarily sourced from pine bark, Pycnogenol's active compounds can also be extracted from alternative sources such as grape seed and peanut skin.

